module IterTools

### Represents a lazy mapping adapter over an input iterable.
### Each source element is transformed only when requested by iteration.
### :typeparam T: The source element type.
### :typeparam U: The projected output type.
### :typeparam S: The concrete source iterable type (borrowed; enables build-time dispatch).
entity SelectIterable[AnyType T, AnyType U, AnyType S] obeys Iterable[U]
needs S obeys Iterable[T]
relates SelectEmittable[T, U, S/Iter] as Iter
  ### Stores the source iterable (borrowed, not owned).
  secret source: Hijacked[S]
  ### Stores the projection routine applied to each value.
  secret transform: Routine[(T,), U]

### Returns the stateful iterator that drives this projection adapter.
### The emitted iterator reuses the same transform routine for every yielded
### source value.
### :returns: The resulting `SelectEmittable[T, U, S/Iter]` value.
@readonly
routine SelectIterable[T, U, S].iter() -> SelectEmittable[T, U, S/Iter]
  danger
    return SelectEmittable[T, U, S/Iter](source: me.source.as_entity().iter(), transform: me.transform)

### Iterates over a source sequence and projects each yielded value through a transform routine.
### :typeparam T: The source element type.
### :typeparam U: The projected output type.
### :typeparam SE: The concrete source iterator type (borrowed).
entity SelectEmittable[AnyType T, AnyType U, AnyType SE] obeys Emittable[U]
needs SE obeys Emittable[T]
  ### Stores the underlying source iterator (borrowed).
  secret source: Hijacked[SE]
  ### Stores the transform routine to apply to each input value.
  secret transform: Routine[(T,), U]

### Returns the next projected value from the mapped sequence.
### The transform runs once for each successfully yielded source value.
### :returns: The resulting `U` value.
routine SelectEmittable[T, U, SE].emit!() -> U
  danger
    var item = me.source.as_entity().emit()
    return me.transform(item)

### Returns a lazy projection of this iterable.
### The source sequence is not evaluated until the resulting iterator is
### consumed.
### :param transform: The routine used to map each source value to a result value.
### :returns: The resulting `SelectIterable[T, U, Me]` value.
@readonly
routine Iterable[T].select[U](transform: Routine[(T,), U]) -> SelectIterable[T, U, Me]
  danger
    return SelectIterable[T, U, Me](source: me.hijack(), transform: transform)
